# Reading the process environment: `var(name)` returns the value of one environment variable.
#
# `std::env` declares no state and opens no source, so a module imports it
# (docs/chl-spec.md, "9.7 Importing asserts no IO and no state"). A call of `var` reads a source in
# the calling module, so the IO belongs to the caller.
#
# The variables a program reads are known when it compiles, and the host reads those variables and
# no others:
#
# - Each name is a string literal, and the compiled program records it with the span of its call.
#   Compiling reads no environment.
# - Before a version starts, the host checks every recorded name against the process environment.
#   A version that reads an unset variable, or one whose value is not UTF-8, is refused with an
#   error at each call that names one, so a missing variable fails the deploy rather than a request.
# - A variable is read once per process. A reload that reads a variable an earlier version read sees
#   the value that version read, and reads a variable it adds when it is installed.
#
# Until the std root is embedded, the prelude's `env_var(name)` is this function, implemented as
# described here (docs/chl-spec.md, "7.3 Sources"). Once `std::env` binds it, the prelude name goes,
# as `http_serve` goes for `std::http::serve`.
#
# Example, an API key used in a request header:
#
#     import std::env
#
#     api_key = env::var("RESEND_API_KEY")
#     auth = {"Authorization": "Bearer " + api_key}
#
# Status: proposed, not in the spec. The std root it belongs to is [Planned] (docs/chl-spec.md,
# "9.16 The std root"). `[proposed]` marks each construct the compiler lacks.

# Returns the value of the environment variable `name`, the one element of its source.
#
# - `name` is a string literal at the call. A name computed at run time is refused, since the host
#   checks every name before the version starts.
# - A value its source does not hold stalls what depends on it, as any absent input does.
# - A call is IO. A module whose top-level evaluation calls `var` is run, not imported
#   (docs/chl-spec.md, "9.7 Importing asserts no IO and no state").
#
# [proposed] binding the intrinsic `__env_var`, which lowering recognizes by identity at the call
# (docs/modules.md, "Intrinsics resolve by identity"), so `name` is the caller's literal; and
# `__env_var`, a name "9.15 Module files" refuses in user modules.
pub var = __env_var
